meta {
  name: 1 Create Sandbox Public Token
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: https://sandbox.plaid.com/sandbox/public_token/create
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "client_id": "{{plaid_sandbox_client_id}}",
    "secret": "{{plaid_sandbox_secret}}",
    "institution_id": "ins_109508",
    "initial_products": ["transactions"]
  }
}

vars:post-response {
  plaid_public_token: res.body.public_token
}

docs {
  # Create Sandbox Public Token

  Mints a Plaid Sandbox `public_token` without going through Plaid Link. This is the same call the integration suite makes in `opulus-tests/integration/backend/helpers/plaidSandbox.ts`.

  **Endpoint:** `POST https://sandbox.plaid.com/sandbox/public_token/create` (calls Plaid directly, not the Opulus backend)

  ## Environment Variables

  - `plaid_sandbox_client_id` (secret): Plaid sandbox client ID
  - `plaid_sandbox_secret` (secret): Plaid sandbox secret

  The institution is hardcoded to `ins_109508` (First Platypus Bank), the same default the integration tests use.

  ## Response

  On success the `public_token` is saved to the `plaid_public_token` variable, which **2 Connect Sandbox Item** reads.

  ```json
  {
    "public_token": "public-sandbox-...",
    "request_id": "..."
  }
  ```

  ## Notes

  - Public tokens are single-use. Re-run this request before each connect.
  - Requires real sandbox credentials from the Plaid dashboard, not the `ci-test` dummies.
}
